  "id": "need-for-closure",
  "term": "need for closure",
  "definition": "Need for closure is a tendency to want a quick, definite answer, leading a person to settle on a judgment rapidly and then resist new information that might change it. Low need for closure involves keeping thinking open and delaying firm conclusions.",
